{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1028044-great-scions-of-fiction","id":1028044,"title":"Great Scions of Fiction!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-06T22:50:21-08:00","id":1028044,"title":"Great Scions of Fiction!","content":"I decided this might be a little less fractious than the &quot;Great Scions of History&quot; thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To kick us off, since my wife has been binging on original-flavor <i>CSI</i> lately, I'll posit Gil Grissom as a Scion of Thoth. (I haven't given <i>too</i> much thought to the others yet, though Jim Brass strikes me as a Scion of Horus...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T09:08:46-08:00","id":1028180,"title":"","content":"Hmm....I kinda had it in my head for a bit that Walter White might be a scion of Tezcatlipoca, having both a keen mind and a penchant for destruction. The fact that he drives an Aztek would probably come up too. Also I will give 500 imaginary Imortan Joe Fun Bucks to whoever has the best argument for which god or goddess bore &quot;Mad&quot; Max Rockatansky. Been thinking about that one for a while...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12598-karasu-sama","name":"Karasu-sama","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T15:26:16-08:00","id":1030825,"title":"","content":"Kvothe, the protagonist of Patrick Rothfuss' Kingkiller novels, might make a good model for a Scion of Hermes. He's a flaming genius, very much a trickster (who sometimes gets caught by his own schemes), an inventor and musician (Hermes invented the lyre, IIRC), and a prodigy at the quasi-scientific magic of his world -- though his obsession is to find the deeper, storybook-style magic of Naming that grants direct control instead of mere redirection of forces. He is also a skilled actor and liar, which adds a level of complexity to the first-person narrative.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T16:53:28-08:00","id":1030862,"title":"","content":"Wonder Woman is absolutely a modern Scion. Depending on which version of her Origin is true,(there's some confusion about that at the moment...) she's either a natural Born daughter of Zeus; or a Construct. Either way, she has the Amazon Template as part of her Path; her mother is Hippolyta, Queen of Themyscira.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T05:09:18-08:00","id":1031094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1028044-great-scions-of-fiction?p=1030825#post1030825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kvothe, the protagonist of Patrick Rothfuss' Kingkiller novels, might make a good model for a Scion of Hermes. He's a flaming genius, very much a trickster (who sometimes gets caught by his own schemes), an inventor and musician (Hermes invented the lyre, IIRC), and a prodigy at the quasi-scientific magic of his world -- though his obsession is to find the deeper, storybook-style magic of Naming that grants direct control instead of mere redirection of forces. He is also a skilled actor and liar, which adds a level of complexity to the first-person narrative.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI actually think Kvothe fits better as a Tuatha scion, maybe of Lugh. He's brilliant, proficient in several fields, a magician and musician of the highest caliber, he's even had dealings with the Fair Folk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T16:15:11-08:00","id":1031868,"title":"","content":"Good point. (I just know Greek myths better than Irish, so that's what I think of first.)<br /> <br /> DS","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T10:58:32-08:00","id":1032211,"title":"","content":"I'd have to second Lugh for Kvothe. For Hermes, I'll go with two characters I just finished reading about....Locke Lamora from Scott Lynch's Gentleman Bastards series and Kaz Brekker from Leigh Bardugo's <i>Six of Crows, </i>a spin-off of her Shadow and Bone trilogy. If you love reading about heists and rogues, I cannot recommend these books enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T20:15:04-08:00","id":1033112,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dx-OXNX4st8\" target=\"_blank\">Skwisgaar Skwigelf taller than a tree.</a><br /> <br /> Fatherklok strongly implies divine ancestry making this crypto-canon! Probably son of Balder or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T06:47:44-08:00","id":1045032,"title":"","content":"Ron Swanson - Scion of an American God of some kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:25:28-08:00","id":1045464,"title":"","content":"You could do a pretty interesting Victorian chronicle with Sherlock Holmes, Allan Quartermain, Dorian Gray, Mowgli, and Mina Harker as Scions. Just not sure who they'd be offspring of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T18:49:19-08:00","id":1045557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1028044-great-scions-of-fiction?p=1045464#post1045464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could do a pretty interesting Victorian chronicle with Sherlock Holmes, Allan Quartermain, Dorian Gray, Mowgli, and Mina Harker as Scions. Just not sure who they'd be offspring of.</div> </div> </div> </div>League of Extraordinary Scions?! I love it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12598-karasu-sama","name":"Karasu-sama","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-na